## Doc map

**This table is the only place a doc path is written down.** `.claude/rules/*`,
`.claude/hooks/*`, skills and agents all defer to it — so moving, renaming or
sharding a doc is a one-file change. Paths are relative to repo root;
`reference/` means `docs/reference/`.

| Working on | Read (on demand → deeper) | Update when it breaks |
|---|---|---|
| {{a code surface, e.g. `backend/app/routers/**`}} | {{the doc to read, shallowest first}} | {{the command to regenerate + the doc to edit}} |
| {{another surface}} | {{…}} | {{…}} |
| a product/domain question | `reference/architecture.md` (domain nouns + invariants) → the one relevant `##` section of `{{product doc}}` | — |

**Docs change only when something breaks a contract** — a response shape, a
schema or access-control decision, an invariant, a route or layout owner, a
design token or component spec. Then the "Update when it breaks" column above
applies. A behaviour-preserving change updates nothing; the Stop hook nudges and
the escape marker is in the **`cook` skill** §10.

**Never a mandated read:** `docs/backlogs/plans/`'s `done/` and `archived/` are
history, and `docs/backlogs/`'s `research/` and `debug/` are write destinations,
not context to load.

**Generated, never hand-edited:** {{list them, with the command that regenerates
each}}. Edit the source and regenerate. The prose docs beside them are
hand-written and stay so — a "why" belongs beside its invariant in
`reference/architecture.md`.

If the area you touched has no row here, ask whether a doc update is needed —
don't silently skip, and don't invent a path outside this table.

